---
// Mount point for lesson 14's workload picker, the phase 3 recap. The intro is
// server-rendered so the lesson still says something without JavaScript.
// Everything after the start button is built at runtime by
// src/scripts/courses/picker/picker.ts.
import "@styles/picker.css";
---

<div data-picker>
  <div class="pw not-prose my-8">
    <div data-pw-stage>
      <div class="pw-shell">
        <div class="pw-body">
          <p class="pw-setup">
            Six things the team needs running. Pick what you'd write for each one. A
            wrong pick tells you what it would actually do, so go ahead and try the
            tempting ones.
          </p>
          <div class="pw-foot">
            <button type="button" class="pw-btn" data-tone="primary" data-go="start"
              >Start</button
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <noscript>
      <p class="pw-note mt-3">
        This needs JavaScript. The short version is two questions. Is it supposed to
        finish? Then it's a Job, or a CronJob on a clock. Does it matter which
        machine it's on or which copy it is? Then it's a DaemonSet or a
        StatefulSet. Otherwise it's a Deployment.
      </p>
    </noscript>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  import "@scripts/courses/picker/picker";
</script>
